LABMIDDLEWARE
Enterprise Technical Documentation
Version: 1.0
Author: Josue Sierra
Repository: https://github.com/JosueSR2

1. OVERVIEW
LabMiddleware is an enterprise-grade laboratory integration middleware designed to interface clinical analyzers with Laboratory Information Systems (LIS) such as OpenELIS.

The system provides protocol-level handling, message transformation, transport abstraction, and secure delivery mechanisms to ensure reliable laboratory data exchange.

Intended for:
- Clinical laboratories
- Hospital environments
- Diagnostic centers
- LIS integration projects
- Analyzer simulation and validation environments
2. SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
Logical Architecture:

Analyzer Layer
      ↓
Transport Layer (TCP / Serial / File)
      ↓
Protocol Engine (HL7 MLLP / ASTM)
      ↓
Parsing & Transformation Engine
      ↓
Delivery Engine (REST API)
      ↓
Laboratory Information System (LIS)

Core Components:
- Transport Listener (TCP, Serial, File Watcher)
- Protocol Processor (HL7 MLLP, ASTM with checksum)
- Message Parser (Segment extraction, result mapping, validation)
- Delivery Engine (REST client, retry policy, batching, circuit breaker)
- Logging & Monitoring (verbosity control, auditing, diagnostics)
3. SUPPORTED COMMUNICATION METHODS
TCP/IP
- HL7 MLLP analyzers
- ASTM over TCP analyzers
Configurable: Port, Encoding, TLS

Serial / USB
- Legacy analyzers
Configurable: PortName, BaudRate, Parity, DataBits, StopBits

File Drop
- Offline analyzers
- Batch export systems
Monitored directory processing
4. SUPPORTED PROTOCOLS
HL7 (MLLP)
Start Block: 0x0B (VT)
End Block: 0x1C (FS) + 0x0D (CR)
Supported segments: MSH, PID, OBR, OBX
Features: UTF-8 support, boundary detection, optional ACK generation

ASTM
Frame structure:
STX | Frame Number | Data | ETX | Checksum | CR LF
Features: Checksum validation, ACK/NAK handling, multi-frame reconstruction
5. CONFIGURATION
Primary configuration file: appsettings.json

Key Configuration Areas:
- LIS endpoint configuration
- Transport activation
- Analyzer-to-port mapping
- Encoding definition
- Retry policies
- Security configuration
6. SECURITY
Supported Features:
- HTTPS (TLS 1.2+)
- Basic Authentication
- Bearer Token Authentication
- Optional certificate validation override
- Configurable HTTP timeouts
- Circuit breaker protection

Recommended Production Setup:
- TLS enabled
- Valid server certificate
- Authentication enabled
- Logging level set to INFO
- Circuit breaker enabled
7. DELIVERY AND RESILIENCE
Delivery Engine Capabilities:
- Configurable retry schedule
- Batched result submission
- Circuit breaker protection
- Timeout configuration
- Outbox persistence (SQLite)

Retry Strategy Example:
10s → 30s → 120s → 300s
8. LOGGING AND MONITORING
Logging Levels:
- ERROR
- WARN
- INFO
- DEBUG

Logs Include:
- Connection events
- Protocol parsing results
- Delivery attempts
- Retry triggers
- Failure diagnostics
9. DEPLOYMENT
Supported Environments:
- Docker container
- Windows Service
- Linux service deployment
- On-premise environments

Recommended Architecture:

Analyzer Network Segment
      ↓
Middleware Server
      ↓
Secure Channel (HTTPS)
      ↓
LIS Server
10. USE CASES
- Hematology analyzer integration
- Biochemistry analyzer integration
- Multi-analyzer hospital environments
- Laboratory simulation platforms
- OpenELIS integration projects
- Analyzer validation labs
